            <ArticleTitle>DNR: &quot;Do Not Resuscitate&quot; or &quot;Death Not Reversible&quot;?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1089/jpm.2017.0466</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allowing physicians to write a do not resuscitate (DNR) or do not administer cardiopulmonary resuscitation order after properly informing patients and their families that death would be irreversible offers a more rational and compassionate approach than traditional shared decision making in establishing a DNR status for some hospitalized patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
